# Comprehensive PR Review Checklist & Code Quality Standards

## Performance Considerations
- Use `find()` instead of `filter()` for single item searches in large arrays
- Implement proper caching strategies for frequently accessed data
- Optimize database queries to avoid N+1 problems
- Consider lazy loading for large datasets
- Minimize bundle size by avoiding unnecessary dependencies
- Add performance monitoring for critical paths

## Code Quality Standards
- Follow consistent naming conventions (camelCase for JS/TS, snake_case for Python)
- Add JSDoc/docstring comments for all public functions and classes
- Maintain maximum function length of 50 lines
- Use meaningful variable names that describe their purpose
- Avoid nested conditionals deeper than 3 levels
- Use interfaces/types with proper prefixes (`I`, `T`)
- Remove unused imports and variables
- Run ESLint and fix all issues

## Validation and Edge Cases
- Handle `null`, `undefined`, and empty values
- Validate all user inputs before processing
- Add error handling for different HTTP status codes
- Dismiss loaders on error conditions
- Provide default values where necessary
- Add edge case testing for error conditions

## Async Code Standards
- Use try/catch blocks with async/await
- Log errors with `console.error()`
- Handle different status codes for fetch operations
- Provide graceful fallbacks
- Implement proper error handling without exposing internal details

## Code Organization
- Use guard clauses for flag-based conditions
- Implement immutable data updates
- Avoid nested if-else chains
- Extract complex logic to services
- Keep PRs focused on single features or bug fixes

## Translation and Messages
- Add translation support for toasts, modals, popups
- Use enums for message constants in CAPITAL_CASE
- Support dynamic content translation

## Subscription Management
- Unsubscribe in `ngOnDestroy` lifecycle
- Use `takeUntil()` pattern for multiple subscriptions
- Implement proper memory leak prevention

## Security Requirements
- Never hardcode API keys, passwords, or sensitive data
- Validate all user inputs before processing
- Use parameterized queries for database operations
- Implement proper error handling without exposing internal details
- Add rate limiting for API endpoints

## Testing Requirements
- Write unit tests for all new functions with minimum 80% coverage
- Include integration tests for API endpoints
- Add edge case testing for error conditions
- Mock external dependencies in tests
- Ensure tests are deterministic and can run independently

## Documentation Standards
- Update README.md when adding new features or changing setup
- Document API endpoints with request/response examples
- Add inline comments for complex business logic
- Keep changelogs updated with user-facing changes
- Include migration guides for breaking changes
- Add JSDoc for complex business logic
- Include usage examples and test cases

## Code Review Readiness
- Write descriptive commit messages following conventional commits
- Ensure all CI/CD checks pass before requesting review
- Remove commented-out code and debug statements
- Add screenshots for UI changes
- Remove `console.log`, `console.warn` (keep `console.error` in catch blocks)

## Accessibility & UX
- Ensure proper ARIA labels for interactive elements
- Maintain color contrast ratios above WCAG AA standards
- Test keyboard navigation functionality
- Add loading states for async operations
- Implement proper error messages for user actions

## Before Submitting PR Checklist
1. Run linting and fix all issues
2. Test edge cases and error scenarios
3. Verify translation support is added
4. Check subscription cleanup
5. Remove debug code and logs
6. Ensure naming conventions are followed
7. Verify all tests pass with minimum 80% coverage
8. Update documentation as needed

## Reminder Instructions
Before generating any code:
1. Review these checklist items and ensure compliance
2. Ask clarifying questions if requirements are unclear
3. Suggest improvements that align with these standards
4. Flag potential issues that might fail PR review
5. Recommend additional tests or documentation needed

When reviewing existing code:
- Identify violations of these standards
- Suggest specific improvements with examples
- Prioritize security and performance issues
- Check for missing tests or documentation gaps